tle:`The Divide Threshold`,subject:`data_structures_algorithms`,topic:`Divide and Conquer: Merge Sort Recurrence`,conceptName:`Merge Sort Recurrence & Two-Pointer Merge`,pathType:`main`,objective:`Divide the input into two equal halves, solve recursively, and merge sorted halves in O(n).`,problemStatement:`Array A[0..n-1] of n elements must be sorted using Divide and Conquer. Recurrence relation: T(n) = 2T(n/2) + Θ(n). Determine the asymptotic complexity and invariant of the 2-pointer linear merge step.`,initialEquationOrState:`T(n) = 2T(n/2) + Θ(n) | Merge Buffer: Unmerged`,targetState:`T(n) = Θ(n log n) | Merged Buffer: A[0..n-1] Monotonically Sorted [D&C VERIFIED]`,correctAnswer:`T(n) = Θ(n log n) with O(n) merge time and O(n) auxiliary space`,optimalSequence:[`DIVIDE_CONQUER`,`MERGE_HALVES`,`BOUND_ASYMPTOTIC`],stepTransformations:[{stepIndex:0,operationKey:`DIVIDE_CONQUER`,resultingState:`Subproblems divided: Left A[0..n/2-1] and Right A[n/2..n-1] with recursion tree depth log2(n).`,explanation:`Split array into two balanced halves of size n/2 and solved subproblems recursively.`,damageValue:45},{stepIndex:1,operationKey:`MERGE_HALVES`,resultingState:`Merged buffer assembled: Two-pointer linear scan merges sorted halves in O(n) comparisons.`,explanation:`Combined two sorted subarrays by comparing leading elements, guaranteeing monotonically sorted output.`,damageValue:50},{stepIndex:2,operationKey:`BOUND_ASYMPTOTIC`,resultingState:`T(n) = Θ(n log n) | Merged Buffer: A[0..n-1] Monotonically Sorted [D&C VERIFIED]`,explanation:`Evaluated Master Theorem Case 2: a=2, b=2 => n^(log2 2) = n^1 matches f(n)=Θ(n), producing Θ(n log n).`,damageValue:50}],validCards:T([`DIVIDE_CONQUER`,`MERGE_HALVES`,`BOUND_ASYMPTOTIC`,`TRACE_ARRAY`,`VERIFY_INVARIANT`]),misconceptions:[],enemy:{name:`Entropy Sorter`,title:`Guardian of Asymptotic Partitions`,hp:220,attack:24,visualType:`algorithmic_horror`,flavorQuote:`Can your shattered halves reconcile before entropy claims the buffer?`},r